# Make a Dragonkin, open the eat menu, refuse to eat a food ration (Dragonkin
# have CA_BURNING_HUNGER and can only feed on blood), and reopen the eat menu.
# This exists for one assertion, inc-i9q.1: a refused meal must not destroy
# the food. Every eat-menu dump below must show the SAME ration count as the
# very first one. Before the fix (src/Item.cpp, Food::Eat) each refusal took
# one ration anyway -- 9 food rations -> 8 -> 7 -> ... -> "food ration"
# (quantity 1) after 8 refusals, on this exact seed and script. See
# tools/check_dragonkin_ration.sh, which reads these dumps and enforces it.
#
# Every choice below is a menu letter, and menu letters move when a list
# changes. Run with a fixed seed or the attribute rolls change, the offered
# feats change with them, and these letters choose something else.
#
# Dragonkin start with a random handful of food rations already in pack (part
# of the shared adventurer starting kit, not race- or class-specific gear --
# see src/Create.cpp). Seed 1 gives 9. Nothing needs to be granted by hand.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes
h       # Race:     [h] Lizardfolk
b       # Subrace:  [b] Dragonkin
a       # Class:    [a] Barbarian
a       # Attributes: the first of the five offered sets
c       # Alignment: [c] Neutral
a       # First feat
a       # Second feat

# Skill Manager, twice. Three RIGHTs per skill spends everything available
# without needing to know how many ranks this character has.
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y

y       # Do you wish to worship <god>? -- yes

RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y

# In the dungeon now. [e] opens "What do you want to eat?"; the only edible
# item Dragonkin start with is the food ration stack, always at [a]. Selecting
# it fires EV_EAT, CA_BURNING_HUNGER refuses it ("Only the blood of a
# carnivorous creature..."), and control returns straight to the map -- no
# further key is needed to dismiss anything. Reopen the menu and dump it, then
# repeat. Eight refusals, matching the bead's measured run.
e
@dump:menu01
a
e
@dump:menu02
a
e
@dump:menu03
a
e
@dump:menu04
a
e
@dump:menu05
a
e
@dump:menu06
a
e
@dump:menu07
a
e
@dump:menu08
a
e
@dump:menu09
ESC
@quit
